# Agent Instructions — {{ project_name }}

Use this file as the entry point for project-level coding rules and coordination conventions. It is the cross-tool conventions file (Codex/OpenCode/etc. read it natively; `CLAUDE.md` imports it for Claude Code). Tool-specific passages are labeled; everything unlabeled applies to every agent.

## Rule Review Requirement

Before implementing changes, review all markdown rule files under `.agents/rules/` (if present in this repo):

1. `.agents/rules/coding_standard.md`
2. `.agents/rules/documentation_style.md`
3. `.agents/rules/formatting.md`
4. `.agents/rules/naming_conventions.md`
5. `.agents/rules/security_guidelines.md`
6. `.agents/rules/restricted_files.md`
7. `.agents/rules/llm_utils_guide.md`

Operational policy: follow those rules as authoritative; prefer reuse from `llm_utils/aiweb_common` before adding new utilities; never expose PHI, credentials, keys, or other secrets in logs, code, docs, or commits.

